[Pipelines > Pipeline Creation Flags > VkPipelineCreateFlags2CreateInfo]
When creating a pipeline, the application can specify a set of flags that control how the pipeline is created and certain aspects of its behavior and capabilities. These flags are specified by chaining the VkPipelineCreateFlags2CreateInfo structure to the pipeline creation structure with a bitmask of VkPipelineCreateFlagBits2, or by setting the flags member of the pipeline creation structure to a bitmask of VkPipelineCreateFlagBits.

The VkPipelineCreateFlags2CreateInfo structure is defined as:

// Provided by VK_VERSION_1_4
typedef struct VkPipelineCreateFlags2CreateInfo {
VkStructureType sType;
const void* pNext;
